Parity disposition (faithful, no scope narrowing):
  - Web <Tabs> is a PURE presentational, fully CONTROLLED primitive (no fetch / React-Query / Promise) -> it has
    NO loading/error/stale/offline branch. Inventing such chrome would FABRICATE states the source does not have,
    so this surface reproduces ONLY the source's REAL branches, exactly as the sibling presentational primitives
    MaskedValue (0220) and Pagination (0221) did. The real branches are:
       * populated  -> the tab strip (web `tabs.map`): each tab rendered selected (accent + 2pt underline, web
                       border-b-2 border-blue-600 text-blue-600) / unselected (muted, hover->primary) / disabled
                       (opacity-50, non-interactive), with roving focus + Left/Right/Home/End automatic-activation
                       keyboard navigation (web handleKeyDown).
       * empty      -> no tabs (web `tabs.length === 0` renders an empty role=tablist container, i.e. a blank box).
                       The native peer instead shows a friendly localized message over the same baseline, satisfying
                       the prompt's "never a blank box" rule. This is the ONLY native prose, lifted into the P1/S10
                       "Tabs" table as `tabs.empty` ("No tabs available").
  - data source `useId` (the only one the prompt lists): reproduced as TabsIdentifiers.generate() — a per-instance,
    render-stable tablist id owned by the controller, carried into {id}-tab-{key} / {id}-panel-{key} element ids
    (web id / aria-controls) so a host can wire its role=tabpanel back to a tab.
  - controlled contract: NO direct HTTP / state in the view. The @Observable TabsController (P1/S8) holds the props,
    derives the projection, and reports activation through the injected `onChange` (web onChange) — gated by the same
    disabled predicate the buttons enforce (a disabled tab's web <button> is `disabled`, so its onClick never fires).
  - keyboard parity: TabsNavigator is the byte-for-byte port of handleKeyDown — enabledKeys-empty -> nil; arrow from a
    non-enabled key (active tab disabled) -> nil (web idx===-1 early return); arrows wrap (idx+delta+n)%n; Home/End jump
    to first/last enabled. The view drives it through onKeyPress(.leftArrow/.rightArrow/.home/.end) on each focused tab.
  - i18n: web routes NO t() literals (tab labels + ariaLabel are caller-supplied, already-localized props, rendered
    verbatim); native ships NO English literals, so the lone added empty-state string resolves through TabsStrings
    (P1/S10). value/label/ariaLabel are rendered verbatim.
  - a11y: the strip is one VoiceOver container (web role=tablist) named by ariaLabel only when present (web aria-label);
    each tab is a button carrying its label + .isSelected when active (web aria-selected) + its tabElementID (web id);
    decorative underline hidden; Dynamic Type via Font.TS; no animation added (web has none) so Reduce Motion is
    inherently respected.
  - tokens: Color.TS.accent/textPrimary/textMuted/border, Font.TS.body(.medium)/label/caption, TSSpacing, TabsLayout
    (Tailwind-metric peers) — NO Tailwind ports, no raw hex. The blue-600 selected hue maps to theme-aware Color.TS.accent.

